# Wireframe: No UI Changes

## Purpose & Flow Context

This change adds containerization (Dockerfile + nginx.conf) at the infrastructure level. It does **not** introduce, modify, or remove any user-facing screens. The built SPA is served by nginx instead of Vite preview or Vercel, but the visual output is identical.

No wireframes are needed because there are zero UI changes.

---

## What Changes

| Layer | Before | After | User Visible? |
|-------|--------|-------|---------------|
| Serving | `pnpm preview` or Vercel | nginx in Docker container | No — same HTML/CSS/JS |
| Deployment | Vercel-only | Docker image + Vercel | No |
| Routing | Vite dev server | nginx `try_files` fallback | No — same behavior |

## Affected Screens

None. All existing screens remain exactly as-is.

## Notes for Implementer

- The nginx configuration must be verified to serve the SPA correctly before considering this complete
- Test by building the Docker image, running it, and navigating through all key app routes
- Verify security headers are present (this is an improvement over the existing setup)
- Verify long-term caching for `/assets/*` files works correctly
